# Working notes — not part of the repo.
# Note `docs/*` rather than `docs/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory itself must stay visible for the
# negation below to work.
docs/*

# THE REFERENCE LEDGER IS NO LONGER TRACKED (2026-08-31, Jesper's decision).
# It carried an exception here on the reasoning that it was "published
# literature values only". That was true of the numbers and false of the
# document: it is a lab notebook that also records provisional readings,
# premises later withdrawn, and mistakes as they happened — deliberately, since
# that record is what stops them being repeated. Read out of context a
# withdrawn premise looks like a claim the project is making.
#
# WHAT UNTRACKING DOES AND DOES NOT DO. It stops FUTURE versions being
# published. It does NOT remove the versions already pushed to this PUBLIC
# repository in commits 8eed20b, ba4429d and ea6d5ac — that would need history
# rewriting, which breaks every existing clone, and was deliberately not done.
# Nothing in the file is patient data or ethics material, so the concern is
# presentational rather than a privacy breach.
#
# The file stays on disk and in use; it is simply local from here on, alongside
# the validation log, backlog and ethics draft.
